            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Portuguese for a jungle, then the Portuguese for a slipper."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: primeiramente",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "primeiramente — \"firstly, first of all\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Primeiramente, abrimos as janelas; depois, limpámos a casa. First of all we opened the windows; then we cleaned the house."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A careful word for speeches and written accounts; in speech people usually say primeiro."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "primeiramente is built on primeiro \"first\", which is inherited from Latin prīmārius \"of the first rank\", from prīmus \"first\" (Lewis & Short), with the adverb ending -mente."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
